989.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said al- Maqburi from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada that his father had said that a man came to the Messenger of Allah
989.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said al- Maqburi from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada that his father had said that a man came to the Messenger of Allah
990.1,"Yahya related to me from Malik, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kuraib, the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, passed by a woman who was in her litter. It was said to her, \This is the Messenger of Allah"
990.2,"Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abu an-Nadr, the freed slave of Umar ibn Ubaydullah, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said about the martyrs of Uhud, \I bear witness concerning these.\"" Abu Bakr as-Siddiq said"
991.1,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from
Talha ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kariyz that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah
bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Shaytan is not considered more
abased or more cast out or more contemptible or more angry on any day
than on the Day of Arafa. That is only because he sees the descent of
the Mercy and Allah's disregard for great wrong actions. That is
except from what he was shown on the Day of Badr."" Someone said, ""What
was he shown on the Day of Badr, Messenger of Allah?"" He said, ""Didn't
he see Jibril arranging the ranks of the angels?"""
991.2,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from
Talha ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kariyz that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah
bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Shaytan is not considered more
abased or more cast out or more contemptible or more angry on any day
than on the Day of Arafa. That is only because he sees the descent of
the Mercy and Allah's disregard for great wrong actions. That is
except from what he was shown on the Day of Badr."" Someone said, ""What
was he shown on the Day of Badr, Messenger of Allah?"" He said, ""Didn't
he see Jibril arranging the ranks of the angels?"""
992.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to say
992.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to say
993.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
993.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
994.1,"[994] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was washed, shrouded, and prayed. Ali, and he was a martyr, may God have mercy on him. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 994 Arabic Hadith:"
994.2,"[994] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was washed, shrouded, and prayed. Ali, and he was a martyr, may God have mercy on him. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 994 Arabic Hadith:"
995.1,"[995] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed: that Omar bin Al-Khattab used to become pregnant in one year. On forty thousand camels, he carries a man to Syria on a camel, and he carries the two men to Iraq on a camel, so he came. A man from the people of Iraq said: Carry me and Suhaim. Then Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said to him: I beseech you, by God, is there a pure blood? He said to him: Yes. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 995 Arabic Hadith:"
995.2,"[995] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed: that Omar bin Al-Khattab used to become pregnant in one year. On forty thousand camels, he carries a man to Syria on a camel, and he carries the two men to Iraq on a camel, so he came. A man from the people of Iraq said: Carry me and Suhaim. Then Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said to him: I beseech you, by God, is there a pure blood? He said to him: Yes. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 995 Arabic Hadith:"
996.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha that Anas ibn Malik had said that when the Messenger of Allah
